{"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0,"metadata":{"colab":{"provenance":[{"file_id":"1lxfPH1p18-HAAO2K0gqV2n2khh8q7lCI","timestamp":1782124420434},{"file_id":"1II7YaS5mnsa1ZM2lpBWWPqNNBa83HAUR","timestamp":1733342319080},{"file_id":"1KR-aAhs5WgpOTOJi5gj2g-MdwnsNCg84","timestamp":1733339632864},{"file_id":"1XDGJKlD1WnpUM3mlJVH_Z5DddRxclAaE","timestamp":1733339494627},{"file_id":"1Q5zOxrKXD8X_2oAQnDlLfGYR0ke0kk68","timestamp":1733338013514},{"file_id":"1y-fAeiu_jsbYJO6YsB5DogZ0t4tFeiML","timestamp":1733319337318}],"gpuType":"T4"},"kernelspec":{"name":"python3","display_name":"Python 3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"},"accelerator":"GPU"},"cells":[{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## 🧠 Environment update — 21 Jan 2026 (Python 3.12)\n","\n","> ⚠️ **IMPORTANT — READ BEFORE RUNNING**\n","\n","Google Colab upgraded to **Python 3.12**.  \n","This notebook **cannot be run top-to-bottom**.\n","\n","You must run **each code block one at a time** and **wait for it to finish** before continuing.\n","\n","**A runtime restart is required after the install cell.**\n","\n","---\n","\n","### Why\n","\n","- **PyTorch / Torchvision upgraded**  \n","  Older versions don’t support Python 3.12.\n","\n","- **NumPy pinned to 1.26.4**  \n","  NumPy 2.x breaks torch / fastai / OpenCV.\n","\n","- **fastai pinned `<2.8.0`**  \n","  The model `.pkl` depends on deprecated `fastcore.transform`.\n","\n","- **Do NOT change system Python**  \n","  It breaks the Colab kernel.\n","\n","---\n","\n","### What to do\n","\n","1. Run the install cell  \n","2. **Runtime → Restart session**  \n","3. Continue with the next cells\n","\n","---\n","\n","> These pins exist only to support legacy `.pkl` models.  \n","> Future models should use **weights-only exports**.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"N1BVAGTkJflL"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["<center>\n","  <a href=\"https://www.sams.ac.uk/science/projects/sea-ai/\" target=\"_blank\">\n","    <img alt='Thumbnail for Sea AI' src=\"https://thredds.sams.ac.uk/thredds/fileServer/images/sea-ai.png\">\n","  </a>\n","</center>\n","\n","<div class=\"markdown-google-sans\">\n","  <p>\n","    This notebook is part of the SEA-AI project which aims to facilitate   cost-effective, accurate, rapid, and consistent seabed-image collection and analysis.\n","  </p>\n","  <p>\n","    This notebook processes transect footage to classify  PMFs using a combination of trained models (YOLOv5 and EfficientNet). The workflow includes video frame extraction, timestamp synchronization with positional data, object detection, and image classification for key PMFs,  maerl,  Burrowing Sea Cucumbers, Horse Mussels, and Northern Sea Fans.\n","  </p>\n","\n","\n","\n","</div>\n"],"metadata":{"id":"N8feHUoa5w0S"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Use of GPU resources\n","\n"," _Before commencing with code execution, it is highly recommended to use a GPU to accelerate the processing and inference steps, particularly when using deep learning models like YOLO and Efficientnet._\n","\n","To enable GPU usage in Google Colab:\n","\n","1. **Change Runtime Type**:\n","- Click on the \"Runtime\" tab at the top of the notebook.\n","- Select Change runtime type from the dropdown menu.\n","\n","2. **Select GPU**:\n","- In the pop-up window, under Hardware accelerator, select GPU from the menu."],"metadata":{"id":"_bY1E5Od1TEJ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Using this notebook\n","\n","<msg desc=\"Text shown above a link to https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V7RXyqFUR98 which highlights some helpful features in Colab\">The information below provides information on usage.</msg>\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"ertVf1iF4Ii6"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## 🚀 What You Need to Do\n","\n","To process footage:\n","Run the cell below to create a folder structure, then upload files to be processed to the input folder, observing the formating instructions below. Cells are run by either selecting the cell then pressing Shift+Enter or clicking the play arrow in the top left of the cell.\n","\n","\n","1. **Upload your video file** to the **input** directory. The Google colab file system is access by the 'file' icon on the left.\n","2. Ensure it is in the correct file format (all common video formats work!) (e.g., `.mp4`, `.mov`).\n","\n","![](https://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&id=1G4FpxaFZgZzVBQFfPyQ0D8mpge-IcaAD)\n","\n","Then\n","1. **Upload your coordinates file** to the **input** directory.\n","2. Ensure it is in the correct format (e.g., `.txt`, `.csv`), and contains data structured as demonstrated below. The date must be in the form of dd/mm/yyyy, the time in the format hh:mm:ss and the coordinates in decimal degrees (WGS84).\n","\n","![](https://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&id=1CUGssBWHcTcqlHDPGeWOlE535WkWswKj)\n","\n","Then\n","1. **Enter a time interval for frame extraction**. Scroll down to find the cell titled 'Time interval for frame extraction' and enter an interval for frame extraction, e.g. 5 (seconds).\n","\n","\n","Then\n","1. **Run all the cells below** (shift+Enter, or use the play buttons) The processing may take a while depending on the footage length. for longer clips please use the SEA-AI executable. This colab is meant as a demonstration.\n","\n","Finally\n","1. **Download the outputs**. ''Video_frames_test' contains the extracted video frames, 'yolo_predict' the frames with object detections and a CSV with the name at the video but with '_out' appended containing the georeferenced detections.\n","\n","![](https://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&id=1qY4Zw9IlirWyo5ncypntB6IdnRXsf-MH)\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"wT0AndUGhNF5"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# Install required packages\n","\n","\n","SEA-AI needs to install prerequisite libraries:"],"metadata":{"id":"plLSqQ_jAeuT"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["!pip install ffmpeg ffmpeg-python opencv-python numpy pandas ffmpeg-python Pillow fastai matplotlib seaborn mplleaflet requests wget opencv-python-headless"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/"},"id":"KjIBgdwHAlmg","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1769008432126,"user_tz":0,"elapsed":25384,"user":{"displayName":"samshabapp","userId":"17072432894550383827"}},"outputId":"820310ba-d90e-48c9-ef38-b2ed8d016d3d"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stdout","text":["Collecting ffmpeg\n","  Downloading ffmpeg-1.4.tar.gz (5.1 kB)\n","  Preparing metadata (setup.py) ... \u001b[?25l\u001b[?25hdone\n","Collecting ffmpeg-python\n","  Downloading ffmpeg_python-0.2.0-py3-none-any.whl.metadata (1.7 kB)\n","Requirement already satisfied: opencv-python in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (4.12.0.88)\n","Requirement already satisfied: numpy in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (2.0.2)\n","Requirement already satisfied: pandas in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (2.2.2)\n","Requirement already satisfied: Pillow in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (11.3.0)\n","Requirement already satisfied: fastai in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (2.8.6)\n","Requirement already satisfied: matplotlib in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (3.10.0)\n","Requirement already satisfied: seaborn in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (0.13.2)\n","Collecting mplleaflet\n","  Downloading mplleaflet-0.0.5.tar.gz (37 kB)\n","  Preparing metadata (setup.py) ... \u001b[?25l\u001b[?25hdone\n","Requirement already satisfied: requests in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (2.32.4)\n","Collecting wget\n","  Downloading wget-3.2.zip (10 kB)\n","  Preparing metadata (setup.py) ... \u001b[?25l\u001b[?25hdone\n","Requirement already satisfied: opencv-python-headless in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (4.12.0.88)\n","Requirement already satisfied: future in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (from ffmpeg-python) (1.0.0)\n","Requirement already satisfied: python-dateutil>=2.8.2 in /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages (from pandas) (2.9.0.post0)\n","Requirement already satisfied: pytz>=2020.1 i